A host must finalize pi's messages and decide finishTurn before any queued
input or further request. Legacy onYield runs before the answer commits and
fabricates a user message to continue; afterTools cannot request an end.

Add an opt-in committed-turn callback and persist its decision in a separate
phase. Recovery before that decision reuses the same entry IDs; callbacks
must be idempotent. Recovery after it never calls the host again. Continue
adds no user message. No callback decision fails closed. Existing paths stay
unchanged without the hook; task version 3 prevents older hosts replaying
the new phases.

Offered upstream as the committed-turn host seam. Apply only to the host's
private pi build; ordinary interactive pi stays unchanged.

